From: FlipperOneEmu
Subject: [PATCH] hw/ufs: a reference clock gating wait time

bRefClkGatingWaitTime (attribute 0x17) read 0, and Linux, which reads
it of a device of UFS 3.0 on, complained at every boot: "Undefined ref
clk gating wait time, use default 255us". The device now says 255 us,
what Linux assumes when it is not said.

---
--- a/hw/ufs/ufs.c	2026-11-26 12:56:22.659030187 -0500
+++ b/hw/ufs/ufs.c	2026-11-26 12:56:22.676771650 -0500
@@ -2832,6 +2832,13 @@
     u->attributes.max_data_in_size = 0x08;
     u->attributes.max_data_out_size = 0x08;
     u->attributes.ref_clk_freq = 0x01; /* 26 MHz */
+    /*
+     * bRefClkGatingWaitTime: a device of UFS 3.0 on says how long it needs
+     * the reference clock before a change of its link's mode, and Linux
+     * reads it (and complains of a 0). 255 us: what Linux assumes when a
+     * device does not say.
+     */
+    u->attributes.ref_clk_gating_wait_time = 0xff;
     /* the configuration descriptor answers (ufs_write_config_desc) */
     u->attributes.config_descr_lock = 0x00;
     u->attributes.max_num_of_rtt = 0x02;
